@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# Native serif peak refinement and grade acceptance
+
+`serif_peaks::Detector` implements the pinned StaffProjector HALF-mode processMultiRestSide boundary for supported multi-line staff geometry. It reuses native projection/threshold setup, then preserves original threshold scanning, browseRange derivative runs, trailing direct createPeak behavior and the acceptance-driven scan position update. Both sides refine the same raw span, with directional tie handling, bounded refinement reach, endpoint fallback and outside chunk minima. LEFT/RIGHT chunk allowances retain the query's added beam thickness.
+
+createPeak retains maximum width, projection maximum, integer-center line ordinates, narrow-column widening, original inclusive vertical-core sampling, interior-gap handling and white-row ratio beyond the serif. Nonzero added chunks select the central half-height core. Six impacts have original weights [1,1,1,1,0.5,0.5], clamp rules and 0.8 intrinsic ratio, with original 0.08 minimum grade. A per-detector work budget bounds searches and raster sampling; unsupported geometry rejects before unsafe access. StaffGeometry supplies actual first/last and middle-line ordinates; the fixture staff is flat with an exact midpoint.
+
+The exact previous original oracle is preserved: 75 SYNTHETIC supplied rasters, not real-score acceptance. All 42 original accepted peaks in 41 positive cases match native encounter order, start/stop/top/bottom and grade within 1e-10. All 34 negative cases produce no native peaks, exactly as the original. Six focused tests across peak acceptance, raster projection and admission pass, along with fmt and all-targets Clippy. The original Java observer, independent inputs, uncompressed outputs and JAR pin are unchanged and inherited from source checkpoint c10a2350; their fixture and observer hashes are recorded. No original/native expected outputs were rewritten to obtain acceptance equivalence.
+
+Equivalence evidence is limited to these 75 flat five-line, interline-16 synthetic controls with added_chunk=6. Sloped/multiple-interline staffs, edge/corner cases, internal pixel-gap variations, other added chunks and real-score serif acceptance still need direct coverage. Full regression at this tree is UNVERIFIED and deferred to the integrated rests boundary; the historical groups-source 275 debug/release checkpoint remains preserved.
+
+Next: integrate actual native staff mapping and serif detection with rest admission, then construct serif filaments/glyphs, register rest and serif inters/relations, and preserve original beam/group cleanup order. Positive complete-rest conversion, epilog, CLI wiring and full OMR remain unfinished.
